## ANSWER KEY & EXPLANATIONS (مفتاح الإجابات والتفسيرات)

### Section A: AI Analytics Answers (إجابات قسم الذكاء الاصطناعي)

| Q# | Answer | Points | Detailed Explanation |
|----|--------|--------|---------------------|
| **1** | **c) 75%** | 1 | Scores below 75% fall into "moderate reliability" zone requiring enhanced monitoring and manual validation. For CRITICAL decisions like 50M DZD orders, minimum 75% is mandatory per training guidelines. Scores 60-74% require additional due diligence. |
| **2** | **b)** | 1 | The Algerian market AI model detects distinct Ramadan pattern: daytime business activity drops ~30% (shorter working hours, fasting), while nighttime activity increases ~40% (post-Iftar shopping peak 20h-23h). This is specifically calibrated for DZ market behavior. |
| **3** | **c) 6** | 1 | Six dimensions evaluated: Product Fit (30%), Location (20%), Capacity (15%), Certification (15%), Price Competitiveness (10%), Performance History (10%). Total = 100%. This weighted approach ensures balanced matching. |
| **4** | **b)** | 1 | Recall = TP/(TP+FN). It measures the model's ability to find ALL actual positives (customers who will churn). 85% recall means 85% of actual churners are correctly identified. Precision (option a) measures quality of positive predictions. |
| **5** | **d) 19%** | 1 | Per Ordonnance 76-147 (Code TVA), the standard/normal rate is 19%. This applies to most goods and services unless specifically listed under reduced (9%) or zero-rated categories. Industrial machinery falls under standard rate. |
| **6** | **c)** | 1 | Conservative scenario uses lower bound of prediction interval (-12 to -15% below central value). This provides safety margin for board presentations and ensures prudent financial planning. Never use optimistic for conservative planning. |
| **7** | **b)** | 1 | System automatically: (1) assigns alert to designated commercial contact, (2) creates CRM priority task, (3) suggests retention actions. It does NOT auto-block, auto-discount, or delete data. Human judgment remains central. |
| **8** | **b) Weekly** | 1 | Demand_Forecast model retrains every Sunday at 02:00. Weekly cadence captures recent trends while avoiding overfitting. More frequent models: Supplier_Matcher (daily); Less frequent: Category_Classifier (quarterly). |
| **9** | **b)** | 1 | Drift = significant change (>5%) in statistical distribution of input data compared to training data. This indicates model may be becoming less accurate as real-world conditions diverge from training conditions. Triggers retraining alert. |
| **10** | **b)** | 1 | Market Share/Penetration strategy recommended for new entrants in competitive markets. Uses lower prices (±3% volatility) to gain initial traction, customer base, and reviews. Can transition to "Optimal Balance" after establishing presence. |
| **11** | **b) False** | 1 | 95% confidence means there's a 95% probability the ACTUAL value falls within the PREDICTION INTERVAL, not that it equals the point prediction. Interval interpretation is crucial - always consider range, not just central value. |
| **12** | **b) False** | 1 | ALL pricing suggestions require human validation before application. This safeguard prevents erroneous extreme suggestions (>15% changes) from being applied automatically. User must click "Apply" after reviewing each suggestion. |
| **13** | **b) False** | 1 | Location is ONE factor weighing 20% of total score. A foreign supplier could score higher overall if they excel in product fit (30%), capacity (15%), certifications (15%), etc. Algorithm optimizes total compatibility, not just location. |
| **14** | **b) False** | 1 | Different primary categories affected: Aïd El-Fitr focuses on clothing/textiles, food, gifts (+200% week before). Aïd El-Adha focuses on livestock/agriculture, different food items (+150%). Coefficients differ by category. |
| **15** | **a) Yes** | 1 | Target error rate threshold is <1%. Therefore 0.5% is well within acceptable range. Error rates 1-5% trigger warning status; >5% is critical requiring investigation. Current system operates at ~0.23% error rate. |

**Section A Subtotal: _____ / 15**

---

### Section B: Compliance Answers (إجابات قسم الامتثال)

| Q# | Answer | Points | Detailed Explanation |
|----|--------|--------|---------------------|
| **16** | **c) 75-89** | 1 | Scores 75-89 qualify as "GOOD" allowing standard processing without additional approval. Scores 90-100 get fast-track. Scores 60-74 require senior operator review. Below 60 requires manager approval or transaction hold. |
| **17** | **b) Ordonnance 75-59** | 1 | Code de Commerce = Ordonnance 75-59 dated September 26, 1975. This is THE foundational commercial law. Option a (03-01) is Foreign Trade Law. Option c (76-147) is TVA Code. Option d (18-07) is Data Protection Law. |
| **18** | **c) Basic cooking oil** | 1 | Basic food necessities qualify for reduced 9% TVA rate: flour, table oil, milk, sugar, semoule. Luxury chocolate (a) is 19%. Machinery (b) is 19%. Smartphones (d) are 19%. Only specific basic necessities get 9%. |
| **19** | **c) Loi 18-07** | 1 | Loi 18-07 dated June 10, 2018 is Algeria's comprehensive data protection law, modeled on GDPR principles. It establishes ANPD (Autorité Nationale de Protection des Données), data subject rights, and processor obligations. |
| **20** | **c) Immediate block** | 1 | EXACT match = confirmed sanctioned entity per OFAC/EU/UN/DZ list. Mandatory immediate blocking of BOTH entity registration AND any pending transactions. No exceptions without CLO approval. This is non-negotiable compliance requirement. |
| **21** | **c) 30 days** | 1 | Maximum acceptable age for RC extract is 30 days. At 25 days (scenario), document is still valid but approaching expiry - system would show warning. At 31+ days, document rejected as expired, requiring fresh extract from CNRC. |
| **22** | **a) 1 hour** | 1 | P1-CRITICAL violations require INITIAL response within 1 hour, resolution within 4 hours. Examples: sanctions exact match, data breach, suspected fraud. P2-MAJOR allows 4 hours initial response. Time is critical for critical violations. |
| **23** | **c) 30 days** | 1 | Per Loi 18-07 (similar to GDPR Article 15), data subjects have right to access their personal data. Platform must respond within 30 days maximum. Extension possible for complex requests (with notification). Best practice: respond within 15 days. |
| **24** | **a) 10%** | 1 | Standard IRG withholding for local service providers is 10%. Note: Rates vary by category - 24% for some consulting services, different rates for freelancers vs companies. Always verify specific service category before applying. |
| **25** | **b) Collect proof docs** | 1 | FIRST step: request identity documentation (full passport, proof of address <3 months, professional certificates). Compare key identifiers (DOB, place of birth, nationality) against sanctioned entry. If DOB differs → likely false positive. Never reveal "you matched sanctions list." |
| **26** | **c) 72 hours** | 1 | Mandatory notification to ANPD within 72 hours of becoming aware of personal data breach. This aligns with international best practices (GDPR requires 72 hours to supervisory authority). Internal documentation and user notification also required. |
| **27** | **b) Loi 03-01** | 1 | Loi 03-01 dated February 26, 2003 governs foreign trade operations including imports, exports, licensing requirements, and customs procedures. This is the primary reference for trade compliance matters. |
| **28** | **c) 30,000,000 DZD** | 1 | Companies with annual turnover exceeding 30 million DZD MUST use monthly TVA declaration regime (déclaration mensuelle). Below this threshold can use quarterly (déclaration trimestrielle). This threshold was updated in recent fiscal reforms. |
| **29** | **b) Politically Exposed Person** | 1 | PEP = Politically Exposed Person. These are individuals who hold/held prominent public positions (government officials, politicians, judicial figures, senior executives of state-owned enterprises). Enhanced due diligence required for PEP relationships. |
| **30** | **c) Destroying/modifying docs** | 1 | Document destruction, modification, falsification, or "updating" during audit is a CRIMINAL offense (obstruction of justice, destruction of evidence). This carries severe penalties including imprisonment. Preparing documents (a), informing legal (b), designating contact (d) are all appropriate. |

**Section B Subtotal: _____ / 15**

